// @run
// @log 2.5
// @log true
// @log z
// @log empty
// @log true
// Regression (silent-class-inventory D1028).
//
// `type JR = Json | E` — a NAME for the composition D1021 closed at its direct spelling.
// Every value arm the recursive alias contributed was delivered raw through the named hop:
// f64 (`found f64`), boolean (`found i32`) and string were check-clean invalid wasm at
// return, binding and argument alike, while the struct arm `E` and `null` — the members the
// COMPOSITION added — ran.
//
// THE MEMBER TABLE IS BUILT FROM THE DECLARED MEMBERS, JOINED VERBATIM. `type JR = Json | E`
// registered the set `Json|E`, so the row held `Json` as ONE opaque atom and the six members
// it stands for were simply absent. Canon flattens the same shape when it sees a whole
// spelling with a pipe in it — which is why the direct `Json | E` runs — but a named alias
// never reaches that loop: canon rewrites a `UnionDecl`'s members one at a time, and a lone
// `Json` has no pipe, so `nameNeedsCanon` declines and the member stays whole. The flatten
// now happens at the declaration site too.
//
// ONLY A MULTI-ATOM EXPANSION IS TAKEN, and the reason is a ruling. A LITUNION alias renders
// through `tyToEmitName` as its SOFTENED base — `type PA = 61 | 62` comes back `i32`, one
// atom — and taking that deletes the arm `is PA` needs, reversing the owner's 2026-07-29
// decision. Three narrower guards were tried first and each was wrong: `nameIsLitUnionType`
// is the string-only twin; `tyIsLitUnion` off `declTyIxOfName` disagrees with the index the
// expander itself resolves; and `unionMemberCount(name)` counts a pipe-joined spelling, so a
// bare alias name answers 1 and rejected every expansion. `literal-unions/
// declared-union-of-litunions.vl` is the file that caught all three.
//
// AND THE SET IS NOT DEDUPED. One entry per member in member order is what the union
// box-tag ABI depends on — `recordUnMemTys` says so in as many words — and a dedupe added
// here silently re-tagged that same litunion file and broke a running program. Measured, not
// reasoned: the dedupe went in, the fixture went red, the dedupe came out.
type Json = null | boolean | f64 | string | Json[] | { [string]: Json }
type E = { at: i32, msg: string }
type JR = Json | E

// The four arms the alias contributes, each read BACK through its narrow — a member table
// that merely accepted the value would still fail here.
function pf(): JR { return 2.5 }
const rf = pf()
if rf is f64 { print(rf) }

function pb(): JR { return true }
const rb = pb()
if rb is boolean { print(rb) }

function ps(): JR { return "z" }
const rs = ps()
if rs is string { print(rs) }

// The two the COMPOSITION adds, which always ran and must keep running.
function pe(): JR { return { at: 0, msg: "empty" } }
const re = pe()
if re is E { print(re.msg) }

function pn(): JR { return null }
print(pn() == null)
